Description: Use a dedicated state group for the internal viewer window
 The internal viewer is a separate KParts::MainWindow. It calls
 setAutoSaveSettings("Viewer", true), but KMainWindow 6.x stores the
 window size, position and state in the "MainWindow" group of the state
 config unless a dedicated group is set. As a result the viewer shares
 the main Ark window's state and does not remember its own size across
 Ark sessions. Give it its own "Viewer" state group.
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-20

--- a/part/arkviewer.cpp
+++ b/part/arkviewer.cpp
@@ -34,6 +34,9 @@
 ArkViewer::ArkViewer()
     : KParts::MainWindow()
 {
+    // Keep the internal viewer's window size/state separate from Ark's main window.
+    setStateConfigGroup(QStringLiteral("Viewer"));
+
     setupUi(this);
 
     KStandardAction::close(this, &QMainWindow::close, actionCollection());
